# iOS simulator storage + no-plaintext-token check — 2026-11-07
Device: simulator "nsh-auth" UDID DEE48BA7-1919-47BC-A04A-887B6D2AB046 (iPhone 18 Pro, iOS 27.0)
App: dev.nshauth.sandbox (NshAuthSandbox.app, Debug-iphonesimulator, built 08:47)

## Storage restart (criterion 6, restart half) — FAILED on this build
1. Signed in via mock loop (04:15Z and twice more); "Status: authenticated",
   access-token tails seen on screen: ...h9Y7, ...Iw-T, ...HehQ.
2. xcrun simctl terminate dev.nshauth.sandbox; relaunch WITHOUT --provider
   (once ~6 min after sign-in, once ~10 s after sign-in; mock access tokens
   are expires_in=3600, so not expiry).
3. Result both times: Sign-in screen ("Sandbox demo: fake client ids..."),
   no session restored. Screenshot: docs/evidence/mock/ios-restart.png.
Root cause read from the built bundle (examples/host-ios/nsh/bundle.js) and
current source: native/ios AuthHostModule stores the session as a JSON STRING
(canonicalValue); packages/nsh-auth/src/host.ts load() returns that string
unparsed, so auth.ts sees expiresAt === undefined, drops and clears it.

## No plaintext token (criterion 6, no-leak half)
Data container: xcrun simctl get_app_container DEE48BA7-1919-47BC-A04A-887B6D2AB046 dev.nshauth.sandbox data
  /Users/hmziq/Library/Developer/CoreSimulator/Devices/DEE48BA7-1919-47BC-A04A-887B6D2AB046/data/Containers/Data/Application/7312127F-437C-49DF-B3D7-F5EF69614175

grep -r -a over the whole container for tails (HehQ / Iw-T / h9Y7) and
prefixes (nsh-sandbox-mock-at-, nsh-sandbox-mock-rt-, nsh-sandbox-):
  ONLY file with hits: Library/Caches/dev.nshauth.sandbox/Cache.db-wal
  (URLSession shared URLCache of the app).
  Contains 3 distinct full access tokens and 3 distinct full
  refresh tokens in plaintext, e.g. the token-endpoint response JSON
  (access_token/refresh_token) and the userinfo request header
  "Bearer nsh-sandbox-mock-at-..." (tails ...h9Y7, ...Iw-T, ...HehQ).
  => "not in any plain file" is VIOLATED by the URL cache WAL. Values are
  fake sandbox tokens of tools/mock-oauth; redacted here to tails.
  nsh Storage module files: no hits anywhere else in the container.
  Keychain (device-level Library/Keychains, NOT inside the app container and
  so outside this grep's reach) is where the app itself keeps the session;
  its items are not plaintext-greppable by design.

